winex11.drv: Copy client surfaces into windows of another process's toplevel.

Only the process that owns a toplevel can attach a client window to its
X window, and it moves, resizes and destroys that window without telling
anyone else. A GPU process drawing for windows of another process (an
embedded WebView2: its GPU process draws for its browser process's
windows) created an onscreen client window that ended up in the wrong
place, or attached nowhere: the page stayed blank, and Chromium's link
preview bubble, a toplevel of the browser process, showed as an empty
white or black box.

Render offscreen and copy into the X window whenever the toplevel belongs
to another process, toplevels included.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/init.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
index 6cca9c4..88e84d7 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
@@ -225,13 +225,22 @@ static BOOL needs_client_window_clipping( HWND hwnd )
 
 static BOOL needs_offscreen_rendering( HWND hwnd, BOOL raw )
 {
+    HWND toplevel = NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_ROOT );
+    DWORD pid;
+
     if (!raw && NtUserGetDpiForWindow( hwnd ) != NtUserGetWinMonitorDpi( hwnd, MDT_RAW_DPI )) return TRUE; /* needs DPI scaling */
+    /* Not in a toplevel of this process: the owner moves, resizes and destroys its X
+     * window without telling us, and only it can attach a client window to it, so ours
+     * would be in the wrong place or nowhere (an embedded WebView2, whose GPU process
+     * draws for windows of its browser process). Copy into its X window instead. */
+    NtUserGetWindowThread( toplevel, &pid );
+    if (pid != GetCurrentProcessId()) return TRUE;
     if (NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT ) != NtUserGetDesktopWindow())
     {
         /* A child window that is shown and that nothing clips can be drawn in its
          * toplevel's X window directly, like a toplevel's own client window. A hidden
          * window has an empty visible region, so it is clipped too. */
-        if (!X11DRV_get_whole_window( NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_ROOT ) )) return TRUE;
+        if (!X11DRV_get_whole_window( toplevel )) return TRUE;
         return needs_client_window_clipping( hwnd );
     }
     if (NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_CHILD )) return needs_client_window_clipping( hwnd ); /* window has children, needs compositing */
